WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.856
Database design comes before trustworthy analysis If
the structure

00:00:05.882 --> 00:00:10.750
is unclear even a syntactically correct query can
produce confusing or unreliable

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:15.095
results That is why we begin by deciding what we are
modeling

00:00:15.121 --> 00:00:20.147
and what one row in each table should mean A
practical design

00:00:20.174 --> 00:00:26.176
process starts with scope What real-world problem
are we representing Then

00:00:26.189 --> 00:00:30.439
we identify the main entities connect them through
relationships and define rules

00:00:30.466 --> 00:00:36.657
that must always hold Normalization helps us reduce
unnecessary repetition

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:42.396
while constraints help prevent invalid data from
entering the database A

00:00:42.422 --> 00:00:46.883
useful final question is this if a different
application inserts data tomorrow

00:00:47.133 --> 00:00:52.056
will the database itself still protect the important
rules Good design should

00:00:52.083 --> 00:00:55.109
not depend only on one user remembering what to do
